          "final_text_tail": "\n\nThe task is complete. Summary of changes:\n\n**`dspy/adapters/types/tool.py`** \u2014 added a `@model_validator(mode=\"before\")` `validate_input` classmethod to `ToolCalls` (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:295) that normalizes varied LM output formats into the canonical structure:\n- **Single object** `{\"name\": ..., \"args\": ...}` (no `tool_calls`) \u2192 wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": [...]}`\n- **Bare list** of tool-call dicts \u2192 wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": <list>}`\n- **Canonical** dict with `tool_calls` key \u2192 passed through unchanged (existing behavior preserved)\n- **JSON strings** \u2192 parsed via `json.loads` and normalized; non-JSON strings returned unchanged\n- **`ToolCalls` instances** \u2192 converted to a plain canonical dict (returns a Python structure, not an instance \u2014 also avoids the base `Type` custom serializer which would stringify via `model_dump()`)\n\n**`tests/adapters/test_tool.py`** \u2014 appended new tests (existing tests untouched): parametrized `validate_input` cases for all formats, a check that an instance input returns a plain dict, and construction tests for single-dict, bare-list, and JSON-string inputs.\n\n**Verification**: all 99 adapter tests pass; full suite 404 passed with only 2 pre-existing litellm failures in `tests/clients/test_lm.py` (confirmed failing on the clean tree too); end-to-end `JSONAdapter` flow verified with mocked LM responses in each format; `ruff check`/`ruff format` clean (the one F811 warning is pre-existing).",
