          "final_text_tail": "\n\nTask complete. The diff is minimal and the full suite is green (336 passed; skips/xfails are pre-existing environmental ones).\n\n**Changes** (`dspy/adapters/types/tool.py`):\n- `_canonicalize_tool_call_args` (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:259) \u2014 recursively sorts dict keys, converts tuples\u2192lists, trims string whitespace, preserves numeric/boolean types (no coercion).\n- `ToolCall` now has `fingerprint: str` and `id: str` fields (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:279-280). Its `__init__` (dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:282) canonicalizes `args` only, builds `{\"name\": ..., \"args\": canonical}` from the validated fields, serializes with `json.dumps(..., sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))`, hashes with SHA-256 \u2192 64-hex-char `.fingerprint`, and stores `.id = fingerprint[:8]` \u2014 computed once at creation, so it's stable for identical calls (any key order / whitespace / tuple-vs-list differences) and always covers `ToolCalls.from_dict_list`, which builds via `ToolCall(**item)`.\n\nVerified: identical calls dedupe to one fingerprint, different names/args/types (`True` vs `1` vs `\"true\"`) differ, `format()` and equality behavior are unchanged, the new fields never leak into LM-facing schemas, and `model_validate`/nested validation paths also trigger `__init__` (pydantic 2.14), so all construction routes get a fingerprint. Added 5 tests to `tests/adapters/test_tool.py` covering format, stability, name/args dependence, type preservation, and `from_dict_list`.",
